  "about": "Port-only (SPEC-menus.md, stages 5 and 7): the campaigns' operations and missions, and the single missions, by the names the remade menus show them. The briefings write them in capitals (FEDCOM:SKYHOOK, ***DESTROY ENEMY CONVOY***); here each in its own case, as the approved frames have them. A mission is its briefing file's (the mission FIT's BriefingFile); an operation is the word its briefings' FEDCOM line gives it. One not here shows as its briefing writes it (logistics/MCMissionNames.h). The match maps (CHOOSE MAP's, the room's), by their room packet's file (data/savegame/*.mpk): 1998's own packets name several by their files' abbreviations (\"CaptIsld\"), the locked ones with LOCKED and two no-artillery ones with NA; here each by its name in words, a locked one with (Locked), the NA ones as their plain maps. One not here (a player's, a mod's) shows by the name its packet holds; the packet's name is still what the room sends. The objectives: a few 1998 objectives' words as the menus say them (\"12 of 12\": \"all 12\"), by the mission's briefing file and the objective's number, where its briefing's line and its mission file's name start with those words.",
